# Commercial S11.1 r2 final-verify rollback diagnosis

Date: 2026-09-20

## Observed boundary

- The r2 backup exists at the authorized immutable backup path with
  `root:root:0700`; checksums and both Git bundles verify.
- The provenance-aware S8 unit started and its health service completed with
  `Result=success`.
- The final contract verification failed closed and the controller restored
  the exact clean source Application and Control commits.
- S11 remained disabled with `live_start IS NULL`; real acquisition and its
  baseline remained present; public services remained active with zero
  restarts.
- Migration 0032 is additive and remains present. Historical latency rows were
  not modified or deleted.

## Root cause

The controller installed the SLO reader under `/usr/local/bin` and invoked it
directly. Its `/usr/bin/env python3` shebang selected system Python. The server
system Python does not provide `psycopg`; the frozen Application virtual
environment does. Consequently the final JSON reader invocation terminated
before returning a contract state and triggered the armed rollback.

The same reader, reconciliation and database return the expected fail-closed
`RED / UNKNOWN_PROVENANCE_FAIL_CLOSED` when invoked with the Application
virtual environment. This proves the SLO contract was not the failure source.
At diagnosis time the database contained twelve immutable legacy
`TECHNICAL_ACCEPTANCE` rows; the additive columns correctly defaulted to
`UNKNOWN`. The versioned reconciliation covers only the six previously proven
rows, so the additional unresolved rows correctly keep the real-user profile
fail-closed. No sample was relabelled or removed.

## Versioned correction and rollback

Bind both the S11.1 contract controller and the later S11 product controller
to the frozen Application virtual-environment interpreter for every installed
reader invocation. Add a static regression test. Do not install a system
package and do not weaken the SLO. The existing r2 rollback and backup are the
recovery path; r1 and r2 freezes remain immutable.
